# ALKIMI Market Making Bot

A production-grade Python asyncio market making bot for the ALKIMI token, running simultaneously on KuCoin, Gate.io, MEXC, and Kraken.

Built on Huy's **Meta Config V1** quant model — an aggressiveness-based, volatility-driven order book depth strategy designed to maximise ALKIMI token + USD treasury holdings rather than notional P&L.

---

## Key Design Goals

| Goal | Mechanism |
|------|-----------|
| Maximise Alchemy token + USD holdings | Inventory-aware skew factor biases buy/sell sides toward initial balance |
| Support price action | Aggressive mode (tight spreads) incentivises trading volume |
| Build treasury via buybacks | Bot accumulates tokens when price is favourable |
| High Sharpe / low drawdown | Circuit breaker, Q-Switch, conservative aggressiveness in high vol |
| Future C++ speed | Exchange connectors sit behind an abstract interface for easy swapping |

---

## Architecture Overview

```
main.py
  ├── Orchestrator          ← fetches prices, computes global mid, runs 4 bots
  │   ├── ExchangeBot (KuCoin)
  │   ├── ExchangeBot (Gate.io)
  │   ├── ExchangeBot (MEXC)
  │   └── ExchangeBot (Kraken)
  ├── FastAPI Server        ← REST + WebSocket monitoring dashboard
  └── SQLite Database       ← orders, fills, inventory snapshots, RL features
```

**Global mid-price formula:**
```
global_mid = 0.45 × Gate + 0.45 × KuCoin + 0.05 × MEXC + 0.05 × Kraken
```
Weights normalise automatically if an exchange is unavailable.

